{
 "indicator": {
  "definition": {
   "definition": "RBI publishes money-market turnover as 'Average Daily Turnover in Select Money Markets' in the Weekly Statistical Supplement, covering call money, notice/term money, triparty repo, market repo and repo in corporate bonds; it also appears daily in the 'Money Market Operations' release as volume measured on one leg, alongside the weighted average rate and rate range. Call money is unsecured borrowing or lending overnight; notice money covers tenors up to and including 14 days; term money covers periods over 14 days and up to one year. Turnover counts both sides of a transaction — twice the single-leg volume for call/notice/term money and triparty repo, and four times for market repo and repo in corporate bonds. The erstwhile Collateralised Borrowing and Lending Obligation segment was replaced by triparty repo with effect from 5 November 2018.",
   "source_name": "RBI Weekly Statistical Supplement — Average Daily Turnover in Select Money Markets (item 12)",
   "source_url": "https://www.rbi.org.in/Scripts/WSSView.aspx?Id=28379",
